summary: Flood the serial console with frequent oom-killer messages, exposing a lockup caused by atomic console contention.
description: |
  https://issues.redhat.com/browse/RHEL-72528

  This test stresses printk subsystem under out-of-memory (OOM) conditions. It
  does so by creating a large number of memory cgroups and launching many
  processes that intentionally exhaust their cgroup's memory limit, triggering
  the OOM killer. At the same time, the test continuously writes long messages
  to /dev/console to generate heavy printk activity.

  It is designed to expose potential deadlocks or stalls in printk, especially
  those related to console locking or memory allocation failures during OOM
  events. The test passes if the system remains responsive and no deadlock
  occurs during the stress period.

contact: Shizhao Chen<shichen@redhat.com>
test: bash ./runtest.sh
framework: shell
require:
  - gcc
duration: 2h
